# Phase 18 factory nullable seven-argument constructor compatibility

- Recorded: 2026-10-23 13:06:13 UTC
- Workspace: `/Users/bruce.tsai/Projects/trio/rocketmq-classic`
- Starting revision: `0d6d9b79`
- Implemented revision: `8f30b6fb`
- Pinned Java source: RocketMQ 5.5.1, `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`
- Scope: nullable seven-argument `MQClientAPIFactory` overload and remoting creator

## Finding and change

The pinned seven-argument constructor accepts a nullable
`ObjectCreator<RemotingClient>`. `MQClientAPIImpl` calls a supplied creator
with the Netty config and channel listener; when the creator is null it builds
the standard Netty client. Both paths still derive the instance name from
`namePrefix + "N_" + index`, so a null prefix yields `nullN_0`.

Core now exposes `new_nullable_with_remoting_client_creator`, which carries
nullable config, prefix, scheduler, and optional creator inputs through the
same factory build path. The Java fixture invokes the seven-argument
constructor with a custom creator and records one invocation plus `nullN_0`.
The Core regression checks the custom creator and the null-creator default
path. Updated fixture SHA-256:
`c0beea285db85680c2c5f68d5786a37dae9f54948e99ccbc2ba5aeef26226a25`.

